# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
SECRET_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# ── Database (Railway sets this automatically via PostgreSQL plugin) ──────────
# Leave blank locally to use SQLite.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dbname

# ── Camera Display Name ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CAMERA_NAME=Main Entrance

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CAMERA SOURCE — pick ONE option below. Leave ALL blank for demo/test mode.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Option A: Phone as IP cam (DroidCam / IP Webcam style) ───────────────────
#
#   HOW IT WORKS (like DroidCam):
#   Your phone runs a local HTTP server on e.g. 192.168.1.50:4747
#   Kafkam runs on Railway (public internet). Your phone is behind your router.
#   To bridge them, expose your phone's server to the internet via a tunnel:
#
#   1. Install "IP Webcam" (Android) or "EpocCam" (iOS) on your phone
#   2. Start the camera server — note the local IP (e.g. 192.168.1.50:4747)
#   3. On the SAME network as your phone, run bore tunnel:
#        npx bore local 4747 --to bore.pub
#      This gives you a public URL like: http://bore.pub:XXXXX
#   4. Set CAMERA_URL to that public URL + /video for MJPEG stream:
#        CAMERA_URL=http://bore.pub:XXXXX/video
#      Or for snapshots only:
#        CAMERA_URL=http://bore.pub:XXXXX/shot.jpg
#
#   DroidCam users: DroidCam serves on port 4747
#        CAMERA_URL=http://bore.pub:XXXXX/video
#
# CAMERA_URL=http://bore.pub:XXXXX/video

# ── Option B: CCTV camera connected via router/switch (RTSP) ─────────────────
#
#   HOW IT WORKS:
#   Your CCTV NVR/camera is on your LAN (e.g. 192.168.1.10).
#   Kafkam on Railway pulls the stream via ffmpeg over the internet.
#   You MUST port-forward 554 (RTSP) on your router to the camera's IP.
#
#   Router config: External port 554 → Internal 192.168.1.10:554
#   Then find your public IP (whatismyip.com) and set:
#
#   Hikvision:   rtsp://admin:password@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP:554/Streaming/Channels/101
#   Dahua:       rtsp://admin:password@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP:554/cam/realmonitor?channel=1&subtype=0
#   Reolink:     rtsp://admin:password@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP:554/h264Preview_01_main
#   Generic:     rtsp://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP:554/stream1
#
# CAMERA_RTSP_URL=rtsp://admin:password@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP:554/stream1

# ── Option C: Both phone cam + CCTV ──────────────────────────────────────────
#   Set CAMERA_RTSP_URL for CCTV (takes priority) AND CAMERA_URL for phone.
#   Currently only one feed is displayed. To switch, comment out RTSP line.

# ── Leave ALL blank → demo mode (animated test pattern, no hardware needed) ──
